msgid ""
"Seconds to wait for the receiver before giving up.\n"
"\n"
"The default of 1 second is deliberately short, and the cost of raising it is paid by a worker: the call is made after the transaction commits, so the request thread is held for however long this allows.\n"
"\n"
"It is also short enough that a receiver which merely thinks for a moment times out, and a timeout here is genuinely ambiguous — the receiver may well have processed the payload. Raise it for a slow but trusted receiver; if delivery has to be certain, this action is the wrong tool (see Webhook URL)."
msgstr ""

